data: {"type":"TOOL_CALL_RESULT","toolCallId":"call_95bb5e1a5a78478ab7fae1c0","messageId":"14e4b606-a44c-4c48-aa86-754de046ef26","content":"{\"ok\":true,\"result\":{\"path\":\"/skills/ui-plugin-development/SKILL.md\",\"content\":\"1: ---\\n2: name: ui-plugin-development\\n3: description: Inspect or customize UI Plugins; implement a new Plugin or new behavior only after a direct user commission, satisfied conditional commission, or approval of a bound development proposal.\\n4: compatibility: Agent UI Plugin Creator Phase 8 permits writes under project plugins and AppUIModel composition.\\n5: allowed-tools: enable_creator_tools takeover_plugin_source ask_user_question read_file ls glob grep edit_file prepare_ui_plugin_development create_ui_plugin mutate_ui_plugin_source prepare_ui_service_contract_change create_ui_service_contract mutate_ui_service_contract inspect_ui_capabilities inspect_ui_plugin_delivery inspect_ui_project inspect_app_ui_model inspect_ui_slots list_ui_plugins inspect_ui_plugin preflight_ui_plugin_placement inspect_ui_services inspect_ui_plugin_source_references inspect_agent_ui_sources apply_agent_ui_source_item mutate_app_ui_model validate_creator_changes\\n6: ---\\n7: \\n8: # UI Plugin development\\n9: \\n10: This Skill applies to frontend Plugin source/application authoring. The system\\n11: prompt owns general evidence, authorization and completion rules; this Skill\\n12: adds Plugin-specific contracts, not an additional investigation checklist.\\n13: Use the smallest relevant section/reference. A resolved existing target does not\\n14: require a full capability inventory, a new UI-system decision or a nearest\\n15: consumer example before it can be modified.\\n16: \\n17: ## Ownership and admission\\n18: \\n19: Project-owned application props, children, renderers and scoped styles are ordinary\\n20: editable code. Inspect the exact target and any concrete unknown contract; edit\\n21: within the user's request. Public npm component use does not require implementation\\n22: source, extraction or takeover. Existing source-owned Plugin edits keep the current\\n23: ownership, upstream provenance and BASE; do not repeat successful takeover consent.\\n24: Only actual npm implementation edits require `takeover_plugin_source` and its\\n25: explicit user agreement. Canonical Runtime/Context, vendor and generated registries\\n26: remain protected. A thin wrapper's omitted public seam is not justification for\\n27: requiring takeover.\\n28: \\n29: Before first new Plugin source or new business behavior, the Host must authorize\\n30: the bounded `prepare_ui_plugin_development` plan. Direct commissions, satisfied\\n31: conditional commissions and approved proposals retain their specific semantics;\\n32: a Skill or inspection does not grant development permission. A normal existing\\n33: Plugin customization does not need a new development approval. For a genuinely new\\n34: Plugin, consult [authoring contracts](references/authoring-contracts.md) for admission,\\n35: manifest/placement, Service/data and delivery obligations. For a new visual Plugin\\n36: or actual UI-system choice also consult [UI selection](references/default-ui-composition.md).\\n37: Do not load new-Plugin investigation requirements for a local presentation repair.\\n38: \\n39: ## Local change evidence\\n40: \\n41: Read the existing files that will change, using the actual supplied sourceRoot and\\n42: owner paths. `manifest.json` declares identity/data/capabilities; `definition.ts`\\n43: joins manifest and component; `index.tsx` owns composition/behavior; imported\\n44: stylesheets own presentation. Read a neighboring consumer only for wiring that\\n45: is actually unknown. An npm implementation need not appear in local search.\\n46: \\n47: `inspect_ui_plugin` returns application ownership, public APIs and parent semantic\\n48: composition where declared. sharedModule selects the installed public module;\\n49: use the root module for presentation controls and /contracts for Plugin types.\\n50: Use returned parameterContracts; follow exact parameterQueries only when a required\\n51: signature is missing. `$element` accesses an array/index element, not React props.\\n52: An unavailable guessed symbol is not a missing capability. Preserve declared\\n53: composition slots when appending controls; replacement props can replace them.\\n54: \\n55: Public types establish invocation shape, not rendered styling. Package-owned\\n56: presentationContract describes raw versus styled components, asset requirements\\n57: and Portal ownership. For a visual defect follow the current owned entry's CSS\\n58: imports and inspect the relevant cascade. Re-querying types cannot establish\\n59: centering. Public overlay composites may own their own Portal and Backdrop;\\n60: respect that composition and retain the existing AgentUIRoot theme container.\\n61: Use the public Trigger/Close/focus APIs. Local dialog state or scoped popup\\n62: positioning does not introduce a Service, Agent action, Runtime replacement or\\n63: source takeover. Verify requested placement, closing and focus in the actual Host.\\n64: \\n65: ## Editing constraints\\n66: \\n67: Freshly read existing edit targets in the current run; old messages/handoff are\\n68: navigation, not current read evidence. `edit_file_from_read` edits a stable range;\\n69: `edit_file` handles small local changes; `mutate_ui_plugin_source` makes one atomic\\n70: Plugin-local transaction with edit/create entries. Re-read and reconcile affected\\n71: files after stale-content errors. Do not hand-edit `registry.generated.ts`, the\\n72: AppUIModel JSON or composition-revision metadata; use their Host tools.\\n73: \\n74: Preserve the target's UI library, enabled capabilities, scope bridge, semantic\\n75: slots and original approval/interrupt/error renderers. New user/screen-reader copy\\n76: uses the unified domain locale namespace with en-US/zh-CN parity; never patch\\n77: vendor for localization. Read locale targets when changing them, not for every\\n78: style edit. Do not invent new per-Plugin i18n or Service abstractions.\\n79: \\n80: Styles must be imported and scoped to owned classes/data attributes; no global\\n81: resets, Host ancestor selectors, Runtime/Portal changes or vendor overrides.\\n82: Own box-sizing, min-width and responsive maximum size. Flex/grid children must\\n83: shrink and long text wrap; overlays need bounded dimensions appropriate to the\\n84: actual container. Static heuristics are not visual acceptance. The specialized\\n85: responsive-repair proposal tool is not currently exposed by any Creator tool\\n86: group. For ordinary authorized responsive CSS changes, freshly read the owned\\n87: stylesheet, use the available file-edit tools and validate the current revision.\\n88: If the user explicitly requests the unavailable specialized proposal tool,\\n89: explain that limitation; do not claim to have invoked it.\\n90: \\n91: ## Validation and outcome\\n92: \\n93: Validate source changes at the current revision; include the build for new visual\\n94: Plugins or dependency/style integration as required. Composition changes use fresh\\n95: AppUIModel evidence and normal Host mutation/verification tools. Creation/catalog\\n96: synchronization is not mounting: newly created capabilities must be composed when\\n97: requested, and the final revision validated. Consume checks already performed by\\n98: the Host rather than duplicating them. Respect returned repair limits.\\n99: \\n100: Keep static, Runtime and browser evidence distinct. Current tests/types or empty\\n101: Runtime errors do not prove popup geometry, keyboard behavior or focus. Validate\\n102: the requested interactions using available authorized browser/test evidence; report\\n103: missing infrastructure or stale evidence precisely. Do not label incomplete work\\n104: as already satisfied or reopen unrelated discovery when verification is unavailable.\\n105: \",\"hash\":\"f9c6297e34d65afd13e854c981b7c058ba5c479da8ff653a87b5448bae741beb\",\"totalLines\":105,\"nextOffset\":null}}","role":"tool"}

