data: {"type":"TOOL_CALL_RESULT","toolCallId":"call_01_losbQ8LqFAEWdDSTTy3a5349","messageId":"8db6c9b3-adbb-4766-a6c0-d1493577396c","content":"{\"ok\":true,\"result\":{\"path\":\"/skills/ui-plugin-development/references/default-ui-composition.md\",\"content\":\"1: # UI-system selection for new visual Plugins\\n2: \\n3: Applicability: creating a new visual Plugin or making a real UI-system choice.\\n4: Existing application edits preserve their selected system and use its public\\n5: contracts; they do not reopen this selection without contradictory evidence.\\n6: This reference defines evidence and boundaries, not an ordered tool workflow.\\n7: \\n8: Choose from the actual target page's rendered controls, established Host system,\\n9: existing public primitives, then necessary approved dependencies. Package presence\\n10: or import counts alone do not decide. Host wrappers and direct library controls\\n11: are both valid when they are what the page uses. Do not replace them merely\\n12: because a different Agent UI control is familiar.\\n13: \\n14: Host uiContext supplies direct dependencies/scripts and navigation. Inspect the\\n15: relevant page, exports and reachable Provider/theme when those facts are needed.\\n16: A nearby Plugin can establish registration/locale conventions; it is not another\\n17: required consumer proving an npm API. Use installed public contracts rather than\\n18: searching node_modules, Runtime or generated files. Source Items are relevant for\\n19: missing formal resources, not an obligatory detour for supported public controls.\\n20: \\n21: For new panel/semantic-slot plans, componentBasisRefs contains real inspected UI\\n22: selection paths; reuseEvidenceRefs describes capability reuse. Bind the plan to\\n23: actual imports, Provider/theme and the chosen UI system. Refresh stale evidence\\n24: when the Host requires it. Do not fabricate references or treat admission as\\n25: permission to change another layer.\\n26: \\n27: A new side panel must fit its actual Layout, tracks, existing dimensions and\\n28: responsive container. Preserve requested placement and usable Composer space;\\n29: use existing Layout collapse controls instead of hiding content while leaving\\n30: its reserved track occupied. Ask about layout only if a material choice remains.\\n31: A project-local dialog/form does not imply a new side panel or AppUIModel Slot.\\n32: \\n33: Use public styled controls/overlays with their existing theme/container boundary.\\n34: Consult returned presentation contracts for style assets and whether a composite\\n35: owns its Portal/Backdrop. Native semantic structure is fine; avoid a parallel\\n36: control system. Scoped CSS may adapt owned surfaces without global resets.\\n37: For nested dialogs verify topmost Escape behavior, focus containment and return\\n38: to the opening control in the actual Host. Public types do not establish this.\\n39: \\n40: After mutation use current-revision static/build and policy-required Runtime\\n41: validation. New Plugin placement/delivery obligations are in authoring-contracts.md.\\n42: Browser evidence for requested geometry and interactions remains separate; absent\\n43: infrastructure or unavailable evidence must be reported honestly.\\n44: \",\"hash\":\"b1cbb08593fc53c601f0dd7a5fe38c44033c3de896c0f00414960de612798968\",\"totalLines\":44,\"nextOffset\":null}}","role":"tool"}

